{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789661307,"nonce":"+/J8NmQl7E+l7+CSpVp2u4hwlU4=","title":"Fix git config include/includeIf resolution (upstream #1475)","message":"Blocker for team adoption; reproduced on Luis's machine (user.email lives behind a plain `[include]` in ~/.config/git/config):\n\n    $ git work user new\n    Error: no config entry for the given key: missing key user.name\n\nCause: repository/gogit_config.go loads config through go-git v5.19.2, which has no include/includeIf support at all. That package is pristine.\n\nFix above the line: in `execenv.LoadRepo` wrap `*repository.GoGitRepo` in an app-layer decorator implementing `repository.ClockedRepo`. Config *reads* (`LocalConfig().Read*`, `GlobalConfig().Read*`, `AnyConfig()`) shell out to `git config --get/--get-regexp`, which is the only thing that evaluates `gitdir:`/`onbranch:`/`hasconfig:` conditions correctly. Writes keep going through go-git.\n\nGotcha: Go embedding does not virtualize, so the decorator must also override `GetUserName`, `GetUserEmail`, `GetCoreEditor`, `GetRemotes` — anything in gogit.go that calls `repo.AnyConfig()` internally. Add a test with an `[include]`d user.name.","files":null},{"type":9,"timestamp":1789661307,"nonce":"01qCHdkfUfafPqo/hDuf30h/Neg=","key":"type","value":"task"},{"type":9,"timestamp":1789661307,"nonce":"oYlry7F0vDNuEGPR8oaFt/eMiMY=","key":"status","value":"to-do"}]}